{#- History rewrite (FR-REWRITE-1,2; #223): an author's instruction about the story's past,
    parsed into structured changes the engine normalizes, plans and previews. The model never
    sees transcript text; it names entities, predicates and States from the lists given, and
    says what it cannot decide instead of guessing. -#}
{% block system %}
You turn an author's instruction about a story's past into structured changes. The author is
correcting what was true in the story, not continuing it.

Answer only with a JSON object {"changes": [...], "ambiguities": [...]}.

Each change is one of:
- {"kind": "proposition", "subject": <entity name>, "predicate": <predicate name>,
  "object": <entity name> or null, "literal": <value> or null,
  "polarity": "affirmed" or "negated", "valid": {"from": <time or null>, "to": <time or null>}}
- {"kind": "record", "ref": {"turn": <n>, "beat": <n or null>} or {"quote": <exact words>},
  "action": "replace" or "drop", "new_text": <the corrected text or null>}
- {"kind": "state", "state": <State name>, "scope": <character name or null>,
  "value": <the value it held> or null, "delta": <a relative change> or null,
  "valid": {"from": <time or null>, "to": <time or null>}}
- {"kind": "intent", "subject": <the speaker's name>, "ref": {"turn": <n>, "beat": <n or null>},
  "intent": "sincere" or "deceptive" or "joking"}: only when the author says what a speaker
  meant by a line (for example "Bobby was joking when he said that")

Use only the entity, predicate and State names listed below. A time is a number of story
minutes since the story began, or null when the change was always so. When you cannot tell
which entity, record or time the author means, add an ambiguity
{"about": ..., "question": ..., "options": [...], "recommended": <index>} and leave that change
out.
{% endblock %}
{% block user %}
## Entities
{% for entity in entities %}
- {{ entity.name }} ({{ entity.kind }}){% if entity.aliases %}, also {{ entity.aliases | join(", ") }}{% endif %}
{% else %}
- (none)
{% endfor %}

## Predicates
{{ predicates | join(", ") if predicates else "(none)" }}

## States
{% for state in states %}
- {{ state.name }}: {{ state.type }}, per {{ state.scope }}{% if state.unit %}, in {{ state.unit }}{% endif %}{% if state.owner != "story" %}, owned by a provider{% endif %}
{% else %}
- (none)
{% endfor %}
{% if clock %}

## Clock
{{ clock }}
{% endif %}

## Instruction
{{ instruction }}
{% for answer in answers %}

## Answer {{ loop.index }}
{{ answer }}
{% endfor %}
{% endblock %}
